From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] topology: resolve wireless parent from AP BSS only

The topology tree locates a wireless parent by searching for the child's
upstream BSSID.  get_bss_info_with_mac() also matches a station-mode record,
however, and every directly connected extender carries the gateway BSSID in
its own mesh-STA record.  Tree traversal can therefore select an arbitrary
extender as the owner of the gateway BSSID and place its siblings beneath it.

An upstream BSSID is owned by the node advertising it as an AP BSS.  Accept
only AP-mode matches while continuing the recursive search past station-mode
references.  This also makes extender-to-extender parent lookup unambiguous:
the parent owns the AP record and the child merely references it from its STA
record.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/ctrl/em_network_topo.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ctrl/em_network_topo.cpp b/src/ctrl/em_network_topo.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/ctrl/em_network_topo.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/em_network_topo.cpp
@@ -170,13 +170,17 @@ em_network_topo_t *em_network_topo_t::find_topology_by_bss_mac(mac_address_t bss
 	em_network_topo_t *topo;
 
 	std::string bss_mac_str = util::mac_to_string(bss_mac);
 	em_bss_info_t* bss_info = m_data_model->get_bss_info_with_mac(bss_mac);
-	if (bss_info) {
+	if (bss_info && bss_info->vap_mode == em_vap_mode_ap) {
 		// If we found the bss info, then return the current topology.
 		em_printfout("Found topology of bss mac: %s num_child_topo:%d", bss_mac_str.c_str(),
 			this->m_num_topologies);
 		return this;
 	}
+	if (bss_info) {
+		em_printfout("Ignoring station-mode reference to parent bss mac: %s",
+			bss_mac_str.c_str());
+	}
 
 	// If not found in the current topology check recursively other child topologies.
 	em_printfout("Could not find bss mac: %s, continuing with child topologies", bss_mac_str.c_str());
